{
 "about": "Pagination and date-window scenarios (appendix A 20, 22, 27, 28, 32 and the plan's stop table). Each scenario serves pages in order: groups of records (only the fields the policy reads: id, created_at UTC, pinned, unavailable; a group is a single post or one module such as a profile conversation) with has_next and cursor (terminated when X ended the timeline), or an error (failed | shape_changed | blocked | login | budget | rate_limited | time_limit). options: limit, since/until as local days YYYY-MM-DD (until is the last day included), tz the local zone they are judged in, chronological whether the surface is newest first by time, server_window when X itself filters by date (search since:/until:), accounts for an account list, save_fails when the resume state cannot be written. start is resumed progress. expected: shown ids in order, stop_reason, pages_fetched, pending (received, not shown, kept for the next handle), window {complete, undated}, continues (a next handle is issued), exit code. A failure after records keeps them. Dates follow the plan's date contract (local days, --until included), an intended change from the previous skill (ISO times, UTC, --until excluded). source: threads contract (the paging and window units are ported), code (previous pagination.py), plan.",
 "scenarios": [
  {
