 "exit_priority": {
  "item": "32,plan",
  "source": "plan (stop table: 5, then the limit, then the deadline) + threads (5 > 4 > 9 > 6)",
  "fact": "When several outcomes apply to one command, the exit code follows: a block a person must clear (5) > login (4) > target unavailable (9) > the operation's limit before any result (10) > other failures (6, or 8 after records). Between the limit and the deadline the first cause that stopped the next request wins; once past the deadline the limit is not weighed again. A tombstone inside a list is a record marker, never exit 9. A batch lookup where nothing resolved: one target is exit 9 (unavailable); several targets are exit 7 with every target listed as unresolved.",
  "order": [
   5,
   4,
   9,
   10,
   6
  ]
 }
}
